From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi: data keys, token categories, token enumerators and object tokens

sapi: data keys, token categories, token enumerators and object tokens

All of these were FIXME stubs returning E_NOTIMPL.

- ISpDataKey on registry keys (data key, token, category): SetData/GetData
  (REG_BINARY; GetData without a buffer reports the size, a short buffer is
  ERROR_MORE_DATA with the size, a missing value SPERR_NOT_FOUND),
  SetDWORD/GetDWORD, DeleteKey (the whole sub tree), DeleteValue,
  EnumKeys/EnumValues (SPERR_NO_MORE_ITEMS at the end). Tokens and
  categories that are not initialized say SPERR_UNINITIALIZED instead of
  dereferencing a NULL key.
- ISpeechDataKey (new, on the data key object): binary, string and long
  values, OpenKey/CreateKey returning data keys, DeleteKey/DeleteValue,
  EnumKeys/EnumValues.
- ISpObjectTokenCategory: GetId, GetDataKey (default location is the
  category's own key; current user, local machine and current config open
  the same path below that root), SetDefaultTokenId (a per-user value) and
  GetDefaultTokenId looking at it before the machine default.
  ISpeechObjectTokenCategory (new, on the category object): Id, Default,
  SetId, GetDataKey, EnumerateTokens.
- ISpObjectTokenEnumBuilder: Skip and Reset, Clone (same tokens, same
  position), AddTokensFromDataKey (the sub keys of a key become tokens
  with ids category\sub key\name), AddTokensFromTokenEnum, and Sort with a
  first token. The IEnumVARIANT of ISpeechObjectTokens gets Skip, Reset and
  Clone; ISpeechObjectTokens gets its IDispatch members and Item.
- ISpObjectToken: all the ISpDataKey members, GetCategory (from the id, up to
  \Tokens or \TokenEnums, or the category given to SetId),
  MatchesAttributes, GetStorageFileName/RemoveStorageFileName (a "Files" key
  of the token remembers the names handed out), Remove (deletes the
  token's key and the caller's storage files), IsUISupported (no UI: FALSE)
  and DisplayUI (SPERR_NOT_FOUND). ISpeechObjectToken: Id, DataKey,
  Category, SetId, GetAttribute, CreateInstance, Remove, storage names,
  UI and MatchesAttributes, and its IDispatch type info members.
- sapi.dll delay-loads shell32 for the storage folders.

